{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Maximum security deposit and annual increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit greater than one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Landlords who collect a security deposit for residential units in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month's rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant entitlement to security deposit interest","requirement":"Interest or earnings on a security deposit belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited toward rent on the lease renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 if written notice was given.","key_value":"Interest paid on renewal/anniversary or January 31","coverage_conditions":"Landlords holding security deposits for residential tenants in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the renewal or anniversary of the tenant's lease or on January 31","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and itemized deductions","requirement":"A landlord must return the security deposit plus interest, less deductions, within 30 days after termination of the tenancy, with an itemized list of any deductions.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; for a broken lease the 30 days starts when the unit is re-rented or the lease expires.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1). Deductions may include the cost of any damages over and above normal wear and tear, and any other money due the landlord under the terms of the lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Expedited security deposit return after displacement","requirement":"A landlord must return the security deposit within five business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation, and tell the tenant where to collect it.","key_value":"5 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within five (5) business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Notice of security deposit account details","requirement":"Within 30 days of receiving a security deposit, and at each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the bank or investment company, the deposit amount, account type and interest rate.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"Landlords holding residential security deposits in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days of receipt of the security deposit and at the time of each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the name and address of the banking institution or investment company in which the money is deposited, the amount of the deposit, type of account, and current rate of interest for the account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after domestic violence lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days after termination.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act due to domestic violence; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals are excluded.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant's security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant's agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
